WEBVTT

00:00:00.079 --> 00:00:01.779
Welcome to Resgrid Academy.

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:06.469
In this lesson, we will understand ai availability and human review.

00:00:07.079 --> 00:00:11.310
AI product descriptions and code can move ahead of deployment availability,

00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:15.159
so training must distinguish released tools from planned ones.

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:18.569
We will explain the features, the setup decisions, and a

00:00:18.569 --> 00:00:20.520
practical way to check the result.

00:00:21.129 --> 00:00:25.180
An administrator asks Admin Assist why a member was not paged and

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:26.749
reviews the evidence it links to.

00:00:27.379 --> 00:00:30.810
Get explanations and drafts for people to review, alongside

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:32.449
the tools you already use.

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:36.329
The examples in this series use a fictional department and are teaching

00:00:36.329 --> 00:00:38.540
scenarios, not default settings.

00:00:39.219 --> 00:00:40.370
Enhanced AI.

00:00:40.899 --> 00:00:44.170
AI assistance beyond the free Admin Assist allowance.

00:00:44.549 --> 00:00:48.299
Nothing to set up yet; your free Admin Assist allowance works without it.

00:00:48.749 --> 00:00:51.490
This feature is marked planned in the source catalog.

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:55.879
Verify release availability before recording a configuration walkthrough.

00:00:56.609 --> 00:01:00.129
The checkout contains gated AI dispatch settings for enrichment

00:01:00.129 --> 00:01:04.490
fields, confidence, sender scope, token limits, and activity.

00:01:04.949 --> 00:01:09.079
Confirm host enablement and department rollout before reviewing the settings.

00:01:09.449 --> 00:01:12.239
Saving settings alone does not start enrichment.

00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:15.800
Check the Running state, activity outcomes, and usage.

00:01:16.189 --> 00:01:19.699
This source-present feature is unverified on the target deployment.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:22.830
Confirm availability in the demo department before

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:24.250
recording the live workflow.

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:27.739
For the training scenario, work in this order.

00:01:28.209 --> 00:01:28.779
Step 1.

00:01:29.349 --> 00:01:33.859
Use deterministic Setup Wizard and Setup Report for configuration guidance.

00:01:34.289 --> 00:01:34.970
Step 2.

00:01:35.510 --> 00:01:38.869
Check whether Admin AI is enabled for the target department.

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:40.090
Step 3.

00:01:40.569 --> 00:01:45.049
Check release and rollout before teaching Enhanced AI summaries or drafts.

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:47.149
Now verify the result.

00:01:47.539 --> 00:01:51.430
Record the target deployment version and observed feature availability.

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:56.460
Human reviewers remain responsible for any generated explanation or draft.

00:01:56.899 --> 00:02:00.469
A common problem to watch for: The catalog in this checkout

00:02:00.469 --> 00:02:02.509
marks Enhanced AI as planned.

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:07.700
This lesson explains its scope; it does not demonstrate a released configuration.

00:02:08.359 --> 00:02:09.920
Your practice task is simple.

00:02:10.399 --> 00:02:14.030
Ask a configuration question through an available tool, inspect

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:18.039
its evidence, and identify any unknowns before making a change.

00:02:18.449 --> 00:02:22.390
Record the result, who owns the follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

